Subject: [PATCH 2/9] test(access): reproduce owner grants surviving demotion
 to operator

3330eb1 makes role-change handling seed the new role's defaults but it
never prunes the old role's. Because role defaults are materialized as
ordinary principal_permission_grants rows, a demoted member keeps them.

Reproducer for the review finding on NEXA-207. Promote operator -> owner,
then demote owner -> operator, and the member still holds the two
owner-only permissions: users:manage_permissions and joins:approve.

users:manage_permissions is the sharper one: a demoted operator can use it
to re-grant themselves the permissions the demotion just removed.

The 28 pre-existing assertions in access-service.test.ts and
access-routes-permissions-upgrade.test.ts all still pass.

