From dfc4d802077b55dddf86eb7d075a37f866cbc578 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jjude80 <18168364+jjude80@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:02:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] NEXA-224: send a client idempotency key with board invoke
 wakes

The board invoke path fired POST /agents/:id/heartbeat/invoke with an empty
body, so nothing reached the idempotencyKey dedupe the route has honoured
since NEXA-194. Board manual wakes already bypass same-scope run coalescing,
which made this the one control path where two presses produced two runs.

Mint one key per in-flight invoke action, per control: presses that land
while an invoke is unresolved reuse the key and coalesce server-side, a
failed request keeps its key so a retry coalesces, and only a settled
success retires it so the next deliberate press starts a new run. The
provider-trace control gets the same treatment.

Tests: two presses of one control now send one key; a later press mints a
fresh key; a failed press reuses its key on retry.
